    "rationale": "Node 7 (current [27,25]) is the rightmost internal node controlling width; moving it left to [23,24] reduces max_x from 27→23, directly shrinking width by 4 tiles. Node 8 moves up to [24,26] into a verified vacancy hotspot (window_21_27_25_31, y=26–27, x=25–27) and aligns vertically with 7’s new y=24 and 11’s target y=30, shortening vertical fanout paths. Node 11 shifts to [23,30] (from [23,31]), exploiting empty tiles above (window_20_26_28_34 shows vacancy at y=30–31, x=20–21) and reducing top extent marginally while preserving output arrival. Swapping 5 and 10 ([22,23]↔[22,25]) co-locates their shared fanin (x2→5, x1→10) and fanout (both →7,10/5), eliminating the long detour on edge [5,7] (9→5 steps in prior certified attempt) and balancing load across y=23–25 band. All moves stay within bounds, avoid collisions, and coordinate internal contraction without moving ports—addressing the failed prior proposal where 2→5 routing exploded (13 steps). This geometry targets measured high-detour edges ([5,7], [4,8]) and uses sparse regions observed in window_21_27_25_31 and window_20_26_28_34."
